{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "op": "ANSWER",
      "refs": ["net_mrr_trend", "net_mrr_current_state"],
      "text": "Net MRR trended $finding:net_mrr_trend.direction across Jan–Dec 2024, with OLS slope of $finding:net_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month (95% CI: $finding:net_mrr_trend.slope_ci95, p = $finding:net_mrr_trend.p_value). Ending the year at $finding:net_mrr_current_state.latest_value in $finding:net_mrr_current_state.latest_period, the business closed $finding:net_mrr_current_state.pct_from_peak off its $finding:net_mrr_current_state.peak_value peak reached in $finding:net_mrr_current_state.peak_period."
    },
    {
      "op": "SECTION",
      "text": "Monthly MRR Components"
    },
    {
      "op": "VIEW",
      "component": "DualAxisChart",
      "series": "monthly_mrr_components",
      "text": "Net, New, Expansion, and Churn MRR — Jan–Dec 2024"
    },
    {
      "op": "EXPLAIN",
      "anchor": "chart_monthly_mrr_components",
      "refs": ["new_mrr_trend", "expansion_mrr_trend", "churn_mrr_trend", "net_mrr_step_change"],
      "text": "New MRR moved $finding:new_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:new_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month (p = $finding:new_mrr_trend.p_value), while expansion MRR followed a $finding:expansion_mrr_trend.direction trajectory at $finding:expansion_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month (p = $finding:expansion_mrr_trend.p_value). Churn MRR drifted $finding:churn_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:churn_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month (p = $finding:churn_mrr_trend.p_value), shaping the net result. No persistent step change survived the detection gates across the year."
    },
    {
      "op": "SECTION",
      "text": "Early vs. Late 2024"
    },
    {
      "op": "TREND",
      "refs": ["net_mrr_split_comparison"],
      "text": "Splitting the year at its midpoint makes the directional shift concrete: the early half ($finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.early_span, n = $finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.early_n months) carried a median net MRR of $finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.early_median, while the late half ($finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.late_span, n = $finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.late_n months) reached $finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.late_median — a $finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.multiplier× step in the central tendency between the two halves."
    },
    {
      "op": "SECTION",
      "text": "What Drove the Change"
    },
    {
      "op": "SHAPE",
      "refs": ["net_mrr_change_decomposition"],
      "text": "Decomposing Dec 2024 vs. Jan 2024, new MRR contributed $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.new_mrr_contribution to the net shift, expansion MRR added $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.expansion_mrr_contribution, and churn exerted a drag of $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.churn_drag. The dominant driver of the full-year change was $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.dominant."
    },
    {
      "op": "SECTION",
      "text": "Plan-Level Breakdown"
    },
    {
      "op": "EXPLAIN",
      "anchor": "chart_plan_mrr_breakdown",
      "refs": ["segment_heterogeneity"],
      "text": "Across Enterprise, Pro, and Starter plans, monthly net MRR levels are significantly different from one another ($finding:segment_heterogeneity.test, p = $finding:segment_heterogeneity.p_value), with per-plan observation counts of $finding:segment_heterogeneity.group_ns. The heatmap below surfaces where within the year each plan contributed most to — or subtracted from — the aggregate trend."
    },
    {
      "op": "CAVEAT",
      "refs": ["grain_plan_check"],
      "anchor": "chart_plan_mrr_breakdown"
    },
    {
      "op": "INSIGHT",
      "refs": ["net_mrr_change_decomposition", "churn_mrr_trend", "expansion_mrr_trend", "net_mrr_split_comparison"],
      "text": "The interplay between a $finding:expansion_mrr_trend.direction expansion trend and a $finding:churn_mrr_trend.direction churn trend is the structural story of 2024: the $finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.multiplier× jump in median net MRR from the early to late half suggests that expansion acceleration outpaced churn growth for long enough to produce a sustained level change, with the decomposition confirming $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.dominant as the single largest lever."
    },
    {
      "op": "METHOD",
      "refs": ["net_mrr_trend", "new_mrr_trend", "expansion_mrr_trend", "churn_mrr_trend", "net_mrr_split_comparison", "net_mrr_change_decomposition", "segment_heterogeneity"],
      "text": "Trends are OLS slopes across the $finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.early_n + $finding:net_mrr_split_comparison.late_n monthly observations in Jan–Dec 2024; the half-year comparison uses median net MRR for robustness to intra-half swings; segment differences are tested with $finding:segment_heterogeneity.test at the plan × month grain confirmed by the data-quality check."
    },
    {
      "op": "CONCLUSION",
      "refs": ["net_mrr_trend", "net_mrr_current_state", "net_mrr_change_decomposition"],
      "text": "Net MRR ended 2024 at $finding:net_mrr_current_state.latest_value, on a $finding:net_mrr_trend.direction OLS slope of $finding:net_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month, driven primarily by $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.dominant — with new MRR contributing $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.new_mrr_contribution, expansion $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.expansion_mrr_contribution, and churn a drag of $finding:net_mrr_change_decomposition.churn_drag against the Jan baseline."
    }
  ]
}
